From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:12:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: ucsi: Don't set the USB state while the partner
 operates in USB4

ucsi_partner_change() puts the port in the USB state when the partner
flags report USB and no Alternate Mode. A partner that has entered USB4
reports USB together with a USB4 flag, so the port is then put in the
USB state although its lanes carry USB4:

  ucsi_connector_change: port1 status: change=0800, ... partner_flags=5
  qcom_usb4_host_mux_set <-typec_mux_set <-typec_set_mode
    <-ucsi_partner_change

A mux that takes the request at its word leaves USB4. One that ignores
it cannot tell it from the real one: when such a partner falls back to
USB 3 by itself (an NVMe enclosure that is given no PCIe tunnel does,
after ten seconds), the flags drop the USB4 bit and the same state is
set, this time correctly:

  ucsi_connector_change: port1 status: change=0800, ... partner_flags=1

When typec_set_mode() was added here, the USB state was set only when
USB was the sole partner flag. The conversion to bitmap accessors turned
that into a test of the USB bit alone. Skip the USB state for a partner
that operates in USB4 as well, as is done for an Alternate Mode.

Fixes: 226ff2e681d0 ("usb: typec: ucsi: Convert connector specific commands to bitmaps")
Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.2
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c | 18 ++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
index 3205877d1..6f2ab54c0 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
@@ -1329,8 +1329,14 @@ static void ucsi_unregister_partner(struct ucsi_connector *con)
 static void ucsi_partner_change(struct ucsi_connector *con)
 {
 	enum usb_role u_role = USB_ROLE_NONE;
+	bool usb4;
 	int ret;
 
+	usb4 = (con->ucsi->version >= UCSI_VERSION_3_0 &&
+		UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB4_GEN4)) ||
+	       (con->ucsi->version >= UCSI_VERSION_2_0 &&
+		UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB4_GEN3));
+
 	switch (UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_TYPE)) {
 	case UCSI_CONSTAT_PARTNER_TYPE_UFP:
 	case UCSI_CONSTAT_PARTNER_TYPE_CABLE_AND_UFP:
@@ -1356,16 +1362,16 @@ static void ucsi_partner_change(struct ucsi_connector *con)
 			typec_set_mode(con->port, TYPEC_MODE_AUDIO);
 			break;
 		default:
-			/* USB and an Alternate Mode can be active together. */
+			/*
+			 * USB and an Alternate Mode can be active together, and
+			 * a partner operating in USB4 reports USB as well.
+			 */
 			if (UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB) &&
-			    !UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_ALT_MODE))
+			    !UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_ALT_MODE) && !usb4)
 				typec_set_mode(con->port, TYPEC_STATE_USB);
 		}
 
-		if (((con->ucsi->version >= UCSI_VERSION_3_0 &&
-		    UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB4_GEN4)) ||
-		    (con->ucsi->version >= UCSI_VERSION_2_0 &&
-		    UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB4_GEN3))) && con->partner)
+		if (usb4 && con->partner)
 			typec_partner_set_usb_mode(con->partner, USB_MODE_USB4);
 	}
 
-- 
